\section{The time-varying setting}\label{section_time_varying}
We now focus on deriving methodology for estimating heterogeneous effects of a time-varying intervention as a function of the history of variables of interest in the currently treated units. For example, the minimum wage might be increased at different times in different counties, and a researcher might wish to study how the effects of wage increases on unemployment vary with poverty rate trajectory leading up to the wage increase and additionally wish to adjust for county demographic variables. We formalize the problem as follows.   

