  & = \frac{1}{D}\sum_{z=1}^D\sum_{y\neq z} \rho_{zy}^{\,t} \leq (D\,{-}\,1)\,\rho_\star^{\,t},
\end{align}
where $\rho_{zy}\,{:=}\,\sum_a\sqrt{p_z(a)\,p_y(a)}$ is the Bhattacharyya coefficient of topics $z$ and $y$, and $\rho_\star\,{:=}\,\max_{z\neq y}\rho_{zy}\,{<}\,1$ by the Cauchy--Schwarz inequality and the distinctness of the topics.
